[2026-10-19T12:14:57.999Z] [INFO]             "text": "It's not installed, but that's okay because the workflow will set it up.\n\n Now, we should also consider that the workflow might need to use the exact same command as the user would run.\n\n We have two steps: one that compiles and runs (which will produce the output) and then another that runs again to verify.\n\n We can combine them, but it's fine.\n\n However, note that the first run (Compile and run HelloWorld) will print the output to the console, which is good for the workflow log.\n\n The second step verifies the output.\n\n We can also just have one step that runs and verifies.\n\n Let's adjust to have a single step that runs and verifies, to avoid duplication.\n\n But the issue says: \"Run the Hello World program\" and \"Verify the output is exactly 'Hello, World!'\".\n\n We can do:\n\n   - run: |\n        output=$(scala HelloWorld.scala)\n        if [ \"$output\" = \"Hello, World!\" ]; then\n          echo \"Test passed\"\n          exit 0\n        else\n          echo \"Expected 'Hello, World!' but got: $output\"\n          exit 1\n        fi\n\n And then we don't need the separate compile step because `scala HelloWorld.scala` will compile and run in one go.\n\n However, note that using `scala` without compiling is fine for a small script.\n\n Let's change the workflow to have only one step after setup that runs and verifies.\n\n We'll keep the checkout and setup, then a single step.\n\n Let's update the workflow.",
