ire a build tool, just a file that can be run with `scala` command.\\n    We'll create it in the root for simplicity, but note that the workflow will need to compile and run it.\\n\\n 2. The program should print \\\"Hello, World!\\\".\\n\\n 3. Add comments and build/run instructions.\\n\\n 4. Create a GitHub Actions workflow in ci/test-hello-world.yml.\\n\\n Let's first check if there are any existing Scala files or directories.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-9b0a8b81-4309-41ca-8f2d-75d65bae37e7\",\"content\":\"\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-e25eed8d-5ad1-466c-8e8c-dd6114cde12d\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"content\\\":\\\"// HelloWorld.scala\\\\n// A simple Scala program that prints \\\\\\\"Hello, World!\\\\\\\"\\\\n//\\\\n// To run this program, you can use the Scala interpreter or compiler:\\\\n//   scala HelloWorld.scala   (for interpreted run)\\\\n//   scalac HelloWorld.scala && scala HelloWorld   (for compiled run)\\\\n//\\\\n// This program follows Scala best practices by using the App trait for a simple main object.\\\\n\\\\nobject HelloWorld extends App {\\\\n  println(\\\\\\\"Hello, World!\\\\\\\")\\\\n}\\\",\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1792411978284/HelloWorld.scala\\\"}\"}}],\"reasoning\":\"No Scala files. Let's create the Scala file.\\n\\n We'll create a simple object with a main method that prints the string.\\n\\n According to Scala best practices, we can use:\\n\\n object HelloWorld extends App {\\n   println(\\\"Hello, World!\\\")\\n }\\n\\n Or the traditional main method.\\n\\n Let's choose the App trait for simplicity.\\n\\n We'll also add a comment at the top with build/run instructions.\\n\\n Since we don't have a build tool, we can just run with `scala HelloWorld.scala`.\\n\\n However, note that the workflow will need to set up Scala. We can use the Scala setup action.\\n