.g., 2.13 or 3.x.\\n\\n We'll use Scala 2.13.12 (a recent 2.13) or 3.3.0. Let's choose 2.13.12 for compatibility.\\n\\n However, note that the user's base branch is e2e/hello-world/39240826691/agent-nemotron-3-super-free, but we are to keep the base branch as that. The workflow should be generic.\\n\\n We'll write the workflow to set up Scala 2.13.12.\\n\\n Steps in workflow:\\n   - checkout\\n   - setup scala\\n   - run the script and check output\\n\\n We can run the script with `scala HelloWorld.scala` and capture the output, then compare.\\n\\n Alternatively, we can compile and run.\\n\\n Let's do:\\n\\n   - scalac HelloWorld.scala\\n   - scala HelloWorld\\n\\n and check the output.\\n\\n We'll use a shell step to run and then use `if` to check.\\n\\n But better to use a step that runs and then uses the exit code to indicate success.\\n\\n We can do:\\n\\n   - run: |\\n        output=$(scala HelloWorld.scala)\\n        if [ \\\"$output\\\" = \\\"Hello, World!\\\" ]; then\\n          echo \\\"Test passed\\\"\\n          exit 0\\n        else\\n          echo \\\"Expected 'Hello, World!' but got: $output\\\"\\n          exit 1\\n        fi\\n\\n However, note that the workflow runs in a Linux environment.\\n\\n Let's create the ci directory and the file.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-22a41850-7ce9-444b-a4c1-49167c873bc9\",\"content\":\"\",\"name\":\"bash\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-b45c39b5-72b4-457e-bfa5-9c7ce77898ee\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"content\\\":\\\"name: test-hello-world\\\\n\\\\non:\\\\n  push:\\\\n    branches: [ main ]\\\\n  pull_request:\\\\n    branches: [ main ]\\\\n\\\\njobs:\\\\n  build-and-test:\\\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\\\n    steps:\\\\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\\\\n      - name: Set up Scala\\\\n        use: coursier/setup-scala@v1\\\\n        with:\\\\n          scala-version: 