[2026-10-19T12:16:45.364Z] [INFO]         "output": "title:\tImplement Hello World in Scala\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\tgithub-actions\nlabels:\t\nassignees:\t\nreviewers:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t3545\nurl:\thttps://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/3545\nadditions:\t40\ndeletions:\t0\nauto-merge:\tdisabled\n--\n## Summary\n\nThis pull request implements a simple Hello World program in Scala and adds a GitHub Actions workflow to automatically test it.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Created `HelloWorld.scala`: a Scala object that prints 'Hello, World!'\n- Added `ci/test-hello-world.yml`: a GitHub Actions workflow that sets up Scala, runs the program, and verifies the output\n\n## How to Test\n\nThe workflow runs on every push and pull request to the main branch. It will:\n\n1. Checkout the code\n2. Set up Scala 2.13.12\n3. Run the Scala script and verify the output is exactly 'Hello, World!'\n\n## Issue\n\nFixes #3544\n\n",
