[2026-10-19T12:17:19.140Z] [INFO]     "text": "I have successfully implemented the Hello World program in Scala and created the required GitHub Actions workflow. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n1. **Created `HelloWorld.scala`**:\n   - A simple Scala object that prints \"Hello, World!\"\n   - Includes clear comments explaining the code\n   - Provides build/run instructions in the file header\n   - Follows Scala best practices using the App trait\n\n2. **Created `ci/test-hello-world.yml`**:\n   - GitHub Actions workflow that triggers on push and pull requests to main branch\n   - Sets up Scala 2.13.12 using the coursier/setup-scala action\n   - Runs the Scala program and verifies the output is exactly \"Hello, World!\"\n   - Located in the `ci/` directory as required\n\n3. **Updated Pull Request #3545**:\n   - Updated title to \"Implement Hello World in Scala\"\n   - Provided detailed description summarizing the changes\n   - Marked the pull request as ready for review\n\n## Verification\n\nThe Scala program has been verified to produce the correct output:\n```\nHello, World!\n```\n\nThe GitHub Actions workflow is configured to automatically run and test the program on every push and pull request to the main branch, ensuring continuous verification.\n\nAll requirements from the issue have been fulfilled, and the pull request is now ready for review.",
